@startuml
title Device State Machine (digital_twin/devices.py)

skinparam backgroundColor #0D1117
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor #1E293B
    BorderColor #334155
    FontColor #F8FAFC
}
skinparam arrow {
    Color #60A5FA
    FontColor #94A3B8
}

[*] --> NORMAL : Device created

state "NORMAL\nrisk: 0.00-0.30" as NORMAL #22C55E
state "WARNING\nrisk: 0.30-0.60" as WARNING #EAB308
state "SUSPICIOUS\nrisk: 0.60-0.80" as SUSPICIOUS #F97316
state "UNDER_ATTACK\nrisk: 0.80-1.00" as UNDER_ATTACK #EF4444
state "OFFLINE" as OFFLINE #64748B

' Manual transitions (validated via STATE_TRANSITIONS table)
NORMAL --> WARNING : transition_to()\nmanual escalation
NORMAL --> SUSPICIOUS : transition_to()\nmanual escalation
NORMAL --> OFFLINE : transition_to()\ndevice down

WARNING --> NORMAL : transition_to()\nrecovery
WARNING --> SUSPICIOUS : transition_to()\nescalation
WARNING --> UNDER_ATTACK : transition_to()\nescalation
WARNING --> OFFLINE : transition_to()\ndevice down

SUSPICIOUS --> NORMAL : transition_to()\nrecovery
SUSPICIOUS --> WARNING : transition_to()\nde-escalation
SUSPICIOUS --> UNDER_ATTACK : transition_to()\nescalation
SUSPICIOUS --> OFFLINE : transition_to()\ndevice down

UNDER_ATTACK --> SUSPICIOUS : transition_to()\nde-escalation
UNDER_ATTACK --> WARNING : transition_to()\nde-escalation
UNDER_ATTACK --> NORMAL : transition_to()\nrecovery
UNDER_ATTACK --> OFFLINE : transition_to()\ndevice down

OFFLINE --> NORMAL : transition_to()\ndevice restored

' ML-driven transitions (bypass validation table)
note right of NORMAL
    <b>ML-Driven Transitions</b>
    (via DigitalTwinStateManager.update_risk_score()
    or record_anomaly() with auto_transition=True)
    
    Risk score directly maps to status:
    • 0.00-0.30 → NORMAL
    • 0.30-0.60 → WARNING  
    • 0.60-0.80 → SUSPICIOUS
    • 0.80-1.00 → UNDER_ATTACK
    
    ML can jump ANY state → ANY state
    based on risk_score from model prediction.
end note

@enduml